{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgubrU3owWayNcjhXcTb4","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I wrote the route to `route.camel.yaml`. I haven't run it against a Camel 4.22 runtime or the SFTP server, so it hasn't been tested.\n\n```yaml\n- route:\n    id: supplier-invoices-sftp-to-file\n    from:\n      id: poll-supplier-sftp\n      uri: sftp://sftp.supplier.example//outbound/invoices\n      parameters:\n        username: trailhead\n        privateKeyFile: /secrets/id_ed25519\n        knownHostsFile: /secrets/known_hosts\n        strictHostKeyChecking: \"yes\"\n        include: '.*\\.csv'\n        delete: true\n        delay: 300000\n      steps:\n        - to:\n            id: write-local-invoices\n            uri: file:work/invoices\n```\n\nNotes:\n- **Absolute path:** the double slash in `//outbound/invoices` makes the path start at the server's root. With a single slash, Camel reads the directory as relative to the login (home) directory.\n- **Host key check:** `strictHostKeyChecking` defaults to `no`, so I set it to `\"yes\"`. Without that, the server's key wouldn't actually be checked against `/secrets/known_hosts`. It's quoted so YAML reads it as text, not true/false.\n- **`.csv` filter:** `include` is a regular expression and is case-sensitive, so a file ending in `.CSV` would be skipped. To accept both, use `'(?i).*\\.csv'`.\n- **Polling interval:** `delay: 300000` is 5 minutes in milliseconds, counted from the end of one poll to the start of the next.\n- **Delete:** with `delete: true`, Camel removes each file from the server only after it has been written to `work/invoices` successfully."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1459,"cache_read_input_tokens":4605,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1459},"output_tokens":582,"service_tier":"standard","inf